# Inert Finance-only native denial provenance

Source/pure only. No SQL/native helper/action/constructor/provider execution, route, PMO denial protocol or public visibility result. Engineering holds remain sticky. This extends the registered Finance reader, not the native permission helpers.

Three fixed callsites only: EARLY_PPE invokes native readable after a true PPE classification; FINAL_RECIPIENT invokes recipient_access after decoded classification agrees; NONSTATEMENT_RECIPIENT invokes recipient_access at entry_checked with no cell. The allowed PD/VE catcher surrounds only the exact helper call. Current inspected native helpers actually raise PD; VE and nonstatement-denial tests are hypothetical boundary-contract stand-ins. Unexpected errors stay fatal.

Before and after each call, exact registered candidate and clean context/phase are checked. A helper that raises/returns after poisoning the entry cannot produce a decision. Successful native denial records fixed pending provenance on its binding ticket; no caller-supplied callback or exception message becomes evidence. Before outcome creation, early denial uses the closed denial_exit scalar identity permit from classified (no transfer); final/nonstatement use existing exit identity. Any identity/context check failure is fatal, not hidden.

Terminal binding record stores callsite and attained phase (classified, decoded or entry_checked). Statement cell becomes denied_unvalidated even after decoded bytes, never falsely final-validated; cell ticket becomes terminal denied. Nonstatement has no cell. No refunds or reset. Existing 100 processing/300 identity permits stay unchanged; early denial uses two identities, final three, nonstatement two. Existing byte/cell/domain reservations stay charged.

A fresh binding ticket can reserve identical metadata from validated OR denied_unvalidated state, then repeats all applicable SIZE/COUNT/CLASS/transfer/decode/final work and native gates with fresh debits. Reserved/live cells and changed metadata hold. The old denied ticket cannot resume, and prior validated evidence is not reused as a later permission result. Same-run distinct bindings still independently run their full checks.

Outcome is private, frozen and repr-suppressed; exact object registration in the marker-owned ledger plus exact original terminal ticket identity is required. It binds actor/PK/normalized keys/default/raw connection, original worklist/row, ticket/callsite/attained phase. Private consumption succeeds once, returns no visibility value, and copied outcomes or wrong contexts fail sticky. The ledger is entry-owned and registration count is capped100. No private native exception text is retained.

20 new pure definitions cover three denial phases, fake VE boundary, copied/one-use outcomes, terminal ticket/provenance, exact retained charges, denied/shared-run full reprocessing, validated→denied, pending/mismatched metadata, native poisoned exception and swallowed-poison return, fatal identity/engineering errors, raw/entry drift. Existing pure gate/cap tests remain; old PPE-denial expectation was deliberately updated from blanket poison to private terminal outcome. Actual SQL/native grant/concurrency/rollback behavior remains UNRUN. Complete visibility composition and PMO's different catch rules remain separate blockers; no full milestone claim.
